The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'bigquery-public-data': {'ebi_chembl': ['products', 'formulations_23', 'formulations', 'products_23']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their usage
• products_23.applicant_full_name : company name to be filtered (= 'SanofiAventis').  
• products_23.product_id          : key that links a product to its formulation(s).  
• products_23.trade_name          : brand / trade name to be displayed.  
• products_23.approval_date       : approval date, keep the most‑recent one per molecule.  
• formulations_23.product_id      : links back to the product.  
• formulations_23.molregno        : ChEMBL molecule identifier (distinct molecule we need).  
Conditions  
• applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis' (exact match).  
• keep only the latest (MAX) approval_date for every molregno.  

Below are ten investigative queries – from very simple exploration to the complete answer – each limited to 20 rows.

```sql
-- 1) List a few company names to see how 'SanofiAventis' appears
SELECT DISTINCT applicant_full_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Show 20 products whose company is exactly 'SanofiAventis'
SELECT product_id, trade_name, approval_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`
WHERE applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Find corresponding formulations for those 20 products
SELECT f.product_id, f.molregno, f.ingredient
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.formulations_23` AS f
WHERE f.product_id IN (
    SELECT product_id
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`
    WHERE applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Join products_23 and formulations_23 to inspect (deduped) molregno–trade_name pairs
SELECT DISTINCT f.molregno, p.trade_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`  AS p
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.formulations_23` AS f
ON p.product_id = f.product_id
WHERE p.applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Add approval_date to observe multiple dates per molecule
SELECT f.molregno, p.trade_name, p.approval_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`  AS p
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.formulations_23` AS f
ON p.product_id = f.product_id
WHERE p.applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
ORDER BY f.molregno, p.approval_date DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Retrieve the most‑recent approval_date per molregno (simple MAX aggregation)
SELECT
  f.molregno,
  MAX(p.approval_date) AS latest_approval_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`  AS p
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.formulations_23` AS f
ON p.product_id = f.product_id
WHERE p.applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
GROUP BY f.molregno
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Same as #6 but keep the corresponding trade_name using ARRAY_AGG & LIMIT 1
SELECT
  molregno,
  (SELECT trade_name FROM UNNEST(trade_names) AS trade_name LIMIT 1) AS trade_name,
  latest_date
FROM (
  SELECT
    f.molregno,
    ARRAY_AGG(DISTINCT p.trade_name) AS trade_names,
    MAX(p.approval_date)            AS latest_date
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`  AS p
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.formulations_23` AS f
  ON p.product_id = f.product_id
  WHERE p.applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
  GROUP BY f.molregno
)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) A row_number() approach to keep only the record with the newest date per molregno
SELECT molregno, trade_name, approval_date
FROM (
  SELECT
    f.molregno,
    p.trade_name,
    p.approval_date,
    ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY f.molregno ORDER BY p.approval_date DESC) AS rn
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`  AS p
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.formulations_23` AS f
  ON p.product_id = f.product_id
  WHERE p.applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
)
WHERE rn = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Bring in ingredient name too, still keeping only the latest approval per molecule
SELECT molregno, ingredient, trade_name, approval_date
FROM (
  SELECT
    f.molregno,
    f.ingredient,
    p.trade_name,
    p.approval_date,
    ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY f.molregno ORDER BY p.approval_date DESC) AS rn
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`  AS p
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.formulations_23` AS f
  ON p.product_id = f.product_id
  WHERE p.applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
)
WHERE rn = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) FINAL ANSWER: Distinct molecules (molregno), their trade name and latest approval date
SELECT
  molregno,
  trade_name,
  approval_date AS latest_approval_date
FROM (
  SELECT
    f.molregno,
    p.trade_name,
    p.approval_date,
    ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY f.molregno ORDER BY p.approval_date DESC) AS rn
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`  AS p
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.formulations_23` AS f
  ON p.product_id = f.product_id
  WHERE p.applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
)
WHERE rn = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

The last query returns one row per molecule associated with the exact company name ‘SanofiAventis’, giving the trade name and the most recent approval date recorded in ChEMBL Release 23.
